      "text": "#thebestofguernsey\n#guernseyairport\n#brittanyferries\n#cheshirehomes\n#guernseylife\n#growlimited\n#mindguernsey\n\nGuernsey in her Glory 😊\n\nLooking for the ultimate festive catch-up?\nSettle in for a lovely atmosphere in the heart of town at Dix-Neuf Brasserie & Bar. We’re ringing in Christmas time with a delicious spread of seasonal sweet treats, freshly brewed tea, and optional prosecco to make your afternoon sparkle.\n\n Festive Afternoon Tea\n Thursday 17th December, from 2pm\n £21 per person\nSpaces are limited and booking is essential—grab your friends and reserve your table today!\nPop in to book with one of our team members.\nPhone +1481 723455\nBook online on our website. See less\n\nThe date was issued at the start of the year, plans are in full swing, venue is booked, caterers are booked, Santa has cleared a space in his diary, the route is set…….\nThis can only mean on thing…….\nThe Guernsey Christmas Tractor Run  – 12th December 2026\n See less\n\nAs the nights draw in, the weather is a bit miserable and its cold outside, if you don't feel like going out, stay in! Jump online and order some tasty snacks, delicious main courses, even some soft drinks. Pick up or have it all delivered straight to your door! See less\n\nThis one is for all the hardworking teams in hotels and restaurants on the island. Once the festive season has quietened down why not have a \"Team Night Out\" Let us do the hard work while you and your teams have a night off and enjoy the hospitality at Le Pommier. Special drink offers and discounts for our fellow industry people for more info and bookings please email events@lepommier.co.uk See less\n\nPlanned road closure\n Rue du Presbytère - Castel\n Monday 16th - Wednesday 18th November\n Electricity service alteration\nWe've approved a request from Guernsey Electricity to close Rue du Presbytère AKA Rectory Hill in Castel from Monday 16th November for three days to allow them to carry out service alteration works.\n If you're cycling, you can still pass through the road closure if done with care and observing dismount signs.\n If you're driving, a diversion will be in place along Rohais de Haut, Rohais de Bas, and Rue des Varendes.\n Details of changes to the scheduled bus routes will be available on the buses app, which can be downloaded in the link in the comments below. See less",
